cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use maneuver-detect in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: maneuver-detect
abstract: >-
  maneuver-detect is a permissively-licensed Python library, a curated open dataset, and a
  frozen benchmark for detecting orbital maneuvers from public TLE history. It assembles a
  labelled mean-element dataset from public catalog data and operator maneuver announcements,
  ships a classical reference detector with a vis-viva / Gauss-variational Δv inversion, and
  defines a leak-free, reproducible benchmark protocol so a new detection method can be measured
  against prior work on the same frozen splits.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dimitrije
    family-names: Jankovic
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/astro-tools/maneuver-detect"
url: "https://github.com/astro-tools/maneuver-detect"
keywords:
  - astrodynamics
  - orbital-mechanics
  - maneuver-detection
  - space-situational-awareness
  - tle
  - benchmark
  - machine-learning
